## ROOT CAUSE (proven, this session)
**8 nodes share each XFS log slice.** test1's replay line:
"foreign replay of dead slot 30 (slice 2/4)" → m_mxfs_log_node_count=4.
Slice index = slot % 4 (xfs_log.c:811 for foreign; xfs_mountfs same
mapping for own mount). 32 nodes on slots 0..31 ⇒ slots 2,6,10,...,30
ALL write slice 2 concurrently. mkfs_mxfs default log_node_count=4
(tools/mkfs_mxfs.c:1479), flag `-n` (line 1490); prep_fs.sh:74 runs
`mkfs_mxfs -f $DEV` with NO -n ⇒ every 32/caw prep formats 4 slices.
The "two inconsistent chains" in slot30_slice.gz are two different
nodes' interleaved log streams (each self-consistent, cycle 1, same
uuid). -EIO at xfs_log_recover.c:1091 is find_tail parsing the soup.

## Evidence chain (all this session)
- Scan of all 1529 headers (scripts/xlog_slice_scan.py, now prints
  uuid + skew): ONE uuid 5fd0a6b2..., ZERO lsn-vs-block skews.
- LUN MXFS super (sector 0, uuid @byte16) = same uuid; prep 19:33:53Z
  ran mkfs unconditionally (prep_fs.sh, FS_PREP_OK, rc=0); gen_uuid =
  /dev/urandom v4 ⇒ H-A (stale residue) REFUTED — all records current
  incarnation.
- test1 FIRST replay attempt 19:35:19 already rc=-5 (journal sweep,
  saved: tool-results/bdq7vzooj.txt) ⇒ corruption existed pre-recovery
  ⇒ not post-death rewrites; concurrent writers during the 19:34 load.
- Covering dummies (7294/7297) need ≥2 idle 30s log-worker ticks —
